@startuml
!include ../style.puml
title Deploy pool, rejected buffer, seed claims, and quarantine
entity "deploy_storage" as Pool <<deploystorage>> {
  * key : raw deploy signature
  --
  value : checked deploy record v2
}
entity "rejected_deploy_buffer" as Rejected <<deploystorage>> {
  * key : raw deploy signature
  --
  value : checked deploy record v2
}
entity "Checked deploy record" as Record {
  magic : F1R3DEP + byte 02
  fingerprint : Blake2b-256(payload), 32 bytes
  payload : signed DeployDataProto protobuf
}
entity "deploy_storage_seeds" as Seeds <<deploystorage>> {
  * key : name seed bytes
  --
  value : signature of the seed holder
}
entity "rejected_deploy_buffer_seeds" as RejectedSeeds <<deploystorage>> {
  * key : name seed bytes
  --
  value : signature of the seed holder
}
entity "deploy_storage_quarantine" as Quarantine <<deploystorage>> {
  * key : original deploy key
  --
  value : original bytes without alteration
}
entity "rejected_deploy_buffer_quarantine" as RejectedQuarantine <<deploystorage>> {
  * key : original deploy key
  --
  value : original bytes without alteration
}
Pool "1" --> "1" Record : decode
Rejected "1" --> "1" Record : decode
Seeds --> Pool : holder signature
RejectedSeeds --> Rejected : holder signature
Pool ..> Quarantine : preserve invalid bytes
Rejected ..> RejectedQuarantine : preserve invalid bytes
note bottom of Quarantine
Quarantine writes precede conditional removal from the live store.
Both copies can exist after an interruption.
Seed claims can require repair after a crash.
These links are not database foreign-key constraints.
end note
legend bottom
Source: key_value_deploy_storage.rs, deploy_codec.rs, deploy_record_quarantine.rs.
The fingerprint detects corruption. Signature verification occurs at the checked write boundary.
endlegend
@enduml
